ontroltype":"Radiocarbon, calibrated"},{"depth":449.5,"geochron":{"agetype":"Radiocarbon years BP","delta13c":-25.6,"delta15n":null,"infinite":false,"percentc":null,"percentn":null,"labnumber":"SUERC-23071","reservoir":null,"geochronid":18314,"geochronage":9205,"geochrontype":"Carbon-14","geochronnotes":null,"percentcollagen":null,"radiocarbonmethod":"accelerator mass spectrometry","geochronerrorolder":41,"geochronerroryounger":41,"geochronmaterialdated":"Higher plant leaf fragments, Empetrum fruit stone and flower bud, Vaccinium myrtillus twigs, Betula nana leaves and seed"},"thickness":2,"agelimitolder":10495,"chroncontrolid":40863,"agelimityounger":10250,"chroncontrolage":10360,"chroncontroltype":"Radiocarbon, calibrated"}]}}],"defaultchronology":11745},"sitedescription":"Glacial origin lake lying within the Risvik sub-stage ice limit and just outside the Outer Porsanger moraine that runs along the ridge to the south of the lake. Site is located in tundra with are dwarf-shrub communities dominated by Empetrum nigrum ssp. hermaphroditum, with Vaccinium vitis-idaea, V. uliginosum, V. myrtillus, and Betula nana as frequent and locally co-dominant components. The local bedrock is mostly dark grey sandstone, alternating with layers of grey-black mudstone and shale, assigned to the Barents Sea group and marginal to the rocks of the Caledonian orogeny."}}],"message":"Retrieved all tables"}